  "content": "ID: G0080\nTitle: Cobalt Group\nURL: https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0080\nCobalt Group is a financially motivated threat group that has primarily targeted financial institutions since at least 2016. The group has conducted intrusions to steal money via targeting ATM systems, card processing, payment systems and SWIFT systems. Cobalt Group has mainly targeted banks in Eastern Europe, Central Asia, and Southeast Asia. One of the alleged leaders was arrested in Spain in early 2018, but the group still appears to be active. The group has been known to target organizations in order to use their access to then compromise additional victims. [1] [2] [3] [4] [5] [6] [7] Reporting indicates there may be links between Cobalt Group and both the malware Carbanak and the group Carbanak . [8]",
  "category": "Article",
  "source": "Local Storage",
